  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Make: Code Your Data Story\r\n\r\nYour Task: Write the code that finds the total and the average of your numbers. Use AI Tutor to draw your picture.\r\n\r\nDo This:\r\n\r\n1. Open `story_plan.txt`. Set `story` and `count` in `main.py` to match your plan.\r\n2. Write your code on the lines marked `YOUR CODE`: start `total` at 0, ask for each number with `input()` (as an `int`), add it to `total`, find the `average` after the loop, and print the total and the average.\r\n3. Ask AI Tutor to draw your picture, using MY AI PROMPT. Paste the code you keep into the `AI SLOT` markers. AI Tutor draws. You write the sum and the average.\r\n4. Predict what your picture will look like, then run your program.\r\n5. Use Validate to check your algorithm.\r\n\r\nChallenge:\r\n\r\nAfter Validate passes, store `total % count == 0` in a variable, print it, and show it in your picture.",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
